  1. Reading, browsing and studying the source code.
  2. Cloning the repository and building the mod for your own personal use.
  3. Quoting parts of the code for analysis, vulnerability reports, security
     reviews, commentary or teaching.
  4. Proposing changes through a pull request on the official repository.
  5. Including the mod in a modpack, and distributing that modpack, provided the
     mod's jar is the unmodified official one, it is offered free of charge, and
     the modpack is not sold or put behind a paywall or an ad-gated download.

WHAT IS NOT ALLOWED without prior written permission from the copyright holder:

  1. Redistributing the mod, compiled or as source, in any form, including on a
